{"name":"Savoy","hex":"#87b550","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Savoy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A historical region shared between the modern countries of France, Italy and Switzerland.","A former duchy existing from 1416 to 1847, whose maximal extent included parts of modern southeastern France, northwestern Italy, and southwestern Switzerland; in full, Duchy of Savoy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Savoy cabbage.","A member of an Italian noble family which became the ruling (hereditary) dynasty of Sardinia and later of Italy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Savoy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Savoy","blocks":[{"text":"Savoy is a cultural-historical region in the Western Alps. Situated on the cultural boundary between Occitania and Piedmont, the area extends from Lake Geneva in the north to the Dauphiné in the south and west and to the Aosta Valley in the east."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Flag_of_Savoie.svg/330px-Flag_of_Savoie.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savoy","wikidata":"Q14118"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Les_Saisies.jpg/500px-Les_Saisies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Les_Saisies.jpg/1280px-Les_Saisies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Les_Saisies.jpg/500px-Les_Saisies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alpine landscape of Les Saisies, as seen from Mont Bisanne.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALes_Saisies.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Karte_Koenigreich_Burgund_DE.png/500px-Karte_Koenigreich_Burgund_DE.png?u